  "workoutName": "W05 Thu Tempo 6mi",
  "description": "TEMPO RUN \u2014 6 miles | Zone 4 (Threshold) | HR 148-155 bpm\n\nPURPOSE: Sustained comfortably-hard effort at your current lactate threshold - trains lactate clearance and the ability to hold a hard pace under control.\n\nFOCUS: Let HR govern the main effort - hold 148-155 bpm (your current Threshold zone, just under LTHR) for the continuous portion. Whatever pace that HR produces today is your honest current tempo pace, not a guess - it'll get faster as fitness improves.\n\nNOTE: 3 continuous miles held in Zone 4 (Threshold, just under LTHR) - controlled hard, not a race. Whatever pace that HR produces is your real current tempo pace.\n\nYOUR DATA: Your last 3 logged runs averaged 121-141 bpm at 8:34-10:17/mi.\n\nFEEL: Comfortably hard - sustainable for the whole segment. Short sentences, not full conversation.",
